<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 2021 source-text-informed nearest tens and hundreds lesson">
  <h2>Warm-up — Estimate the number-line point</h2>
  <p>Use the original 2021 number-line picture supplied by your teacher. Discuss a too-low, about-right and too-high estimate. The original point position was not independently image-verified and has no auto-graded exact answer.</p>
  <h2>Activity 1 — Find the nearest multiple of 100 and of 10</h2>
  <p>Locate each original source number on a properly scaled 100-wide number line. Complete the two nearest-multiple columns; your teacher checks point placement and reasoning.</p>
  <table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Source number</th><th>Nearest 100</th><th>Nearest 10</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr><td>128</td><td>100</td><td>130</td></tr><tr><td>272</td><td>300</td><td>270</td></tr>
  <tr><td>436</td><td>400</td><td>440</td></tr><tr><td>89</td><td>100</td><td>90</td></tr>
  <tr><td>351</td><td>400</td><td>350</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <p>For 128, the two surrounding tens are 120 and 130. Because 128 is 8 from 120 and 2 from 130, choose 130.</p>
